From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Lam <matthew.lam@openrouter.ai>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:21:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Make pstack work in Claude Code and Codex

Upstream now maps Cursor names to Claude Code in docs/harness/claude-code.md.
Only what it leaves broken stays here:
1. poteto-mode points Claude Code at that adapter. Upstream adds the
   pointer only to its generated harness tree, which this repo does not
   vendor, so without it Claude Code never reads the adapter.
2. Codex has no upstream adapter. poteto-mode names its role file and
   transcripts; without them Codex ignores Matthew's roles and the
   transcript-reading skills find nothing.
3. The adapter runs non-Claude roles through the host's cross-provider
   tool or codex exec. Upstream runs them on the session model, which
   collapses the two-family review panel Matthew's rules require.
4. worktree-audit.sh also searches Claude Code and Codex transcripts.
   Without it a worktree a live session still uses is bucketed safe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 plugins/pstack/docs/harness/claude-code.md                | 2 +-
 plugins/pstack/skills/poteto-mode/SKILL.md                | 2 ++
 .../pstack/skills/poteto-mode/scripts/worktree-audit.sh   | 8 ++++++--
 3 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plugins/pstack/docs/harness/claude-code.md b/plugins/pstack/docs/harness/claude-code.md
index bf154e6..9a780a4 100644
--- a/plugins/pstack/docs/harness/claude-code.md
+++ b/plugins/pstack/docs/harness/claude-code.md
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@ pstack skills use Cursor names. In Claude Code, read this file once per session,
 | Cursor | Claude Code |
 | --- | --- |
 | `claude-<family>-<version>-<effort>[-fast]`, such as `claude-opus-5-5-xhigh` | `model: "opus"` and `effort: "xhigh"`. `model` takes only `opus`, `sonnet`, `haiku`, `fable`. Drop `-fast`. |
-| A `grok-*`, `gpt-*`, or other non-Claude slug | Omit `model` so the agent runs on the session model, and say so. |
+| A `grok-*`, `gpt-*`, or other non-Claude slug | Run that seat through the host's cross-provider tool, such as T3 Code's `delegate_task`, or `codex exec -m <slug>`. Omit `model` and say so only when neither works. |
 | `auto` or `inherit-parent` | Omit `model`. |
 | The `pstack-models.mdc` rule, `~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc` | `~/.claude/rules/pstack-models.md`. Claude Code loads it into every new session, so its role lines are already in context. If they are not, read the file. If the file or the role's line is missing, use the skill's default slug. |
 | A role value `<model> <effort>`, such as `opus high` | `model: "opus"` and `effort: "high"`. |
diff --git a/plugins/pstack/skills/poteto-mode/SKILL.md b/plugins/pstack/skills/poteto-mode/SKILL.md
index 21993f5..c241a13 100644
--- a/plugins/pstack/skills/poteto-mode/SKILL.md
+++ b/plugins/pstack/skills/poteto-mode/SKILL.md
@@ -10,6 +10,8 @@ color: yellow
 
 Bundled skills live at `../<name>/SKILL.md` from this file, so put this file's absolute path in every `poteto-agent` prompt.
 
+<!-- tool-neutral: start -->In Claude Code, read [the Claude Code adapter](../../docs/harness/claude-code.md) once per session before you follow this skill. In Codex, the `pstack-models.mdc` rule is `~/.claude/rules/pstack-models.md`, and transcripts are the rollouts under `~/.codex/sessions/` whose `session_meta` `cwd` is this workspace.<!-- tool-neutral: end -->
+
 ## Non-negotiables
 
 The Principles section below grounds every trigger. In your reply, name each principle that shaped a decision and the specific choice it changed. Cite only principles whose leaf SKILL.md you read this session.
diff --git a/plugins/pstack/skills/poteto-mode/scripts/worktree-audit.sh b/plugins/pstack/skills/poteto-mode/scripts/worktree-audit.sh
index 47e0891..cda7af0 100755
--- a/plugins/pstack/skills/poteto-mode/scripts/worktree-audit.sh
+++ b/plugins/pstack/skills/poteto-mode/scripts/worktree-audit.sh
@@ -72,6 +72,9 @@ fi
 # Transcripts dir: ~/.cursor/projects/<slugified-repo-path>/agent-transcripts.
 slug=$(printf '%s' "$main_wt" | sed 's#^/##; s#/#-#g')
 transcripts="$HOME/.cursor/projects/$slug/agent-transcripts"
+# Also ~/.claude/projects/*/*.jsonl and ~/.codex/sessions/.
+other_transcripts=()
+for d in "$HOME/.claude/projects" "$HOME/.codex/sessions"; do [ -d "$d" ] && other_transcripts+=("$d"); done
 now=$(date +%s)
 
 echo "# base: $base"
@@ -111,8 +114,9 @@ git worktree list --porcelain | awk '/^worktree /{print $2}' | while read -r wt;
 	# Most recent chat whose transcript operated in this worktree. Match path
 	# followed by "/" or a quote so glint-482 does not match glint-482-r37.
 	last="-"; last_ts=0
-	if [ -d "$transcripts" ]; then
-		f=$(rg -l -e "${wt}/" -e "${wt}\"" "$transcripts" 2>/dev/null \
+	search=(${other_transcripts[@]+"${other_transcripts[@]}"}); [ -d "$transcripts" ] && search=("$transcripts" ${search[@]+"${search[@]}"})
+	if [ "${#search[@]}" -gt 0 ]; then
+		f=$(rg -l -e "${wt}/" -e "${wt}\"" "${search[@]}" 2>/dev/null \
 			| xargs stat "${stat_fmt[@]}" 2>/dev/null | sort -rn | head -1)
 		if [ -n "$f" ]; then last_ts=$(echo "$f" | awk '{print $1}')
 			last=$(fmt_day "$last_ts" 2>/dev/null); fi
